********************************************************************************
SharedMeatAxe Version 1.0                                                 README
********************************************************************************

This is an autotoolized shared library version of C MeatAxe 2.4.24, a set of
programs for computing with modular representations.

See INSTALL for installing shared_meataxe-1.0.

The package comprises a shared library "libmtx", as well as several
executables.

See COPYING for licence information.

Arithmetic tables
-----------------
By default, configure selects DATADIR/meataxe (normally PREFIX/share/meataxe)
as the library's arithmetic table directory. Use --with-mtxlib=DIR to select
a different directory. The resolved path is compiled into libmtx and its
programs, and is available through pkg-config --variable=mtxlibdir libmtx.

Table generation and installation are disabled by default, as in earlier
releases; --disable-tables explicitly selects this behavior. Packagers can
enable them with --enable-tables. In that mode, make generates the tables for
all prime powers from 2 through 256 in the build tree; make install copies them
to the configured directory, respecting DESTDIR. Installed programs and library
clients can then read the tables without setting MTXLIB or having write access
to the installation directory. When tables are disabled, packagers must provide
them separately or users must choose a writable table directory for runtime
generation.
The programs still accept MTXLIB and -L/--mtxlib as runtime overrides, with
the command-line option taking precedence. Library clients can override the
default by setting MtxLibDir before performing finite-field operations.

